1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,333
Hello everyone

2
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:06,066
Today we are going to play one more good old classic, FTB Ultimate

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,500
Which is also the pack where I first encountered GregTech

4
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:14,966
Anyways, we shall quickly get started with a new world

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,900
And we spawned close to a village that seems to not have any loot chests

6
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,333
After a quick peek at it

7
00:00:22,366 --> 00:00:25,300
We get started and do the usual vanilla stuff

8
00:00:25,866 --> 00:00:28,966
Meaning we rush a bed and then gather some materials

9
00:00:29,466 --> 00:00:31,666
Now that we have a bed and some food

10
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:33,800
We can go gather some minerals

11
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,066
And that should be enough to get our base started

12
00:00:54,466 --> 00:00:58,066
And the first thing we shall do is get some building materials

13
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,266
We are going to make our base with the good old trusty stone bricks

14
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,966
And after some work

15
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:07,666
Here we have our new shelter with a nice window on the sky

16
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:12,133
Now we can start processing the minerals with an old pulverizer

17
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,400
This is from before the introduction of Forge Energy

18
00:01:15,666 --> 00:01:18,166
Back when we used Minecraft Joules

19
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:21,266
Now, before moving on with our factory

20
00:01:21,366 --> 00:01:23,200
We shall get some proper tools

21
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:24,900
Such as a Power Armor

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,666
This armor doesn't even look cool in that version

23
00:01:27,766 --> 00:01:29,566
And as we made it

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,066
It only provides a different cosmetic

25
00:01:32,166 --> 00:01:33,933
To make it have any use

26
00:01:34,066 --> 00:01:36,166
We need a Power Armor tinker table

27
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:40,266
That requires one emerald which we didn't find while mining

28
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,733
But luckily, villagers trades exist in that version

29
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:45,800
And that guy has a nice offer

30
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,500
We accept this quest from the guild hall

31
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,333
And quickly proceed to fill it

32
00:01:50,566 --> 00:01:53,700
And thus we have our tinkers table to tweak our armor

33
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,900
Inside that we can see our armor equipped modules

34
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,300
And we can add, remove or edit them

35
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:04,300
The first thing we want is to add some plating so that it provides some Protection

36
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,800
We quickly craft the material required for the upgrade

37
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,500
And proceed into installing it into our armor

38
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:14,466
Next, we can choose how thick we want our plating to be

39
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,000
The more thick the more protection we gain

40
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:20,133
But we also have more weight to carry around

41
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,500
Since we want to be well-protected

42
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:26,566
We install it at maximum defense on each part of our armor

43
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:31,300
And thus we have an unbreakable armor as good as a diamond one but made out of iron

44
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,066
The issue is that it's heavy

45
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,733
To workaround that

46
00:02:34,866 --> 00:02:40,466
We can install some augmentations on our leggings to help us walk with all of that weight

47
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:46,833
And again, we can tweak how powerful and in what way these augmentations shall help us walk

48
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,733
However, these require power

49
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,600
So we also have to install a battery

50
00:02:51,966 --> 00:02:54,500
Which is going to increase further up our weight

51
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,666
And of course, we need some generators to charge up our batteries

52
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:05,100
However, all of the generators we can embed in our armor require control circuits

53
00:03:05,366 --> 00:03:06,800
Which require glowstone

54
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,700
Before going into the nether

55
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:10,366
We craft a power tool

56
00:03:10,566 --> 00:03:12,700
Which will make any other tool obsolete

57
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,666
Freeing a lot of hotbar space

58
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:18,933
This robotic arm can do about everything you could need

59
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,400
Such as the basic mining tools

60
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,266
To get the obsidian

61
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,533
We can upgrade it with some diamonds

62
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:30,466
And we should probably overclock the pick feature at the maximum for that task

63
00:03:30,466 --> 00:03:34,800
And thus we can now punch obsidian with our bare robotic hands

64
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:39,266
Before going into the nether, we should get some more cool features

65
00:03:39,266 --> 00:03:40,333
Such as a rail gun

66
00:03:40,666 --> 00:03:42,900
Or maybe we can get that later on

67
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,266
For the moment let's make a melee assistant be enough

68
00:03:46,666 --> 00:03:50,166
Then we fully charge our armor with an IC2 generator

69
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,966
Once we are fully charged and equipped

70
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,333
We proceed into another expedition

71
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,800
Where our only objective shall be gathering a couple of glowstone dusts

72
00:04:00,733 --> 00:04:03,866
We quickly accomplish the mission and then run back

73
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:05,533
With that rushed loot

74
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,500
We can finally make a couple of HV capacitors

75
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:12,133
And thus we can install a railgun in our robotic hand

76
00:04:12,533 --> 00:04:13,933
And of course

77
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,100
We crank it at maximum power

78
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,100
The railgun has two main purposes

79
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,933
One is to be used as a long range weapon

80
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,566
But the most important one

81
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:28,666
Is that we can use it to fly around by using its kickback

82
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
And thus we were able to quickly find a desert

83
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,800
Where we can gather the other missing ingredient for the control circuits, cactus

84
00:04:37,266 --> 00:04:40,500
And with that we can have a solar generator on our helmet

85
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:44,000
And we can also get night vision goggles

86
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:48,166
Then an auto-feeder so that we won't have to manage food

87
00:04:48,966 --> 00:04:51,733
And an electrolyzer for when we go diving

88
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:56,000
But the real cool thing is getting a kinetic generator

89
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,500
This will produce energy when we walk

90
00:04:58,566 --> 00:05:00,600
But it will make walking harder

91
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:04,700
However, it produces more than the exoskeleton assistant uses

92
00:05:05,866 --> 00:05:07,333
But this is a techpack

93
00:05:07,466 --> 00:05:09,300
So enough fooling around

94
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:13,466
We shall make a bunch more of the old Thermal Expansion machines

95
00:05:14,666 --> 00:05:17,666
And we shall use these to expand our base

96
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:22,666
Since the real machines, the GregTech ones, will need more space

97
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:26,133
And while we wait for the building materials

98
00:05:26,366 --> 00:05:28,800
We can do some more resource gathering

99
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:33,500
But it looks like it is going to take a while more for the basic processing stuff

100
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:40,100
So we shall use that time to go gather more ender pearls in the end for some more armor upgrades

101
00:05:40,566 --> 00:05:42,533
And on our way to the end

102
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:44,133
We found a dungeon

103
00:05:44,533 --> 00:05:46,266
While exploring the dungeon

104
00:05:46,466 --> 00:05:48,300
We found one more fun toy

105
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:49,333
A portal gun

106
00:05:49,966 --> 00:05:52,400
This is one more memory of great game's

107
00:05:52,566 --> 00:05:54,266
For those of you who don't know

108
00:05:54,333 --> 00:05:59,400
This item allow us to create portals on the walls so that we can easily move around

109
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:03,766
It can also be used to move around any mob or item

110
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:10,500
And yes, its best usage was to troll people when playing on multiplayer servers

111
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,066
Anyways, going back to our adventure

112
00:06:13,266 --> 00:06:16,266
Once we managed to find and complete the end portal

113
00:06:16,366 --> 00:06:18,566
We started gathering some ender pearls

114
00:06:19,166 --> 00:06:22,066
But when we had enough and wanted to go back

115
00:06:22,133 --> 00:06:27,166
We found out that the portal gun was not going to bring us away from that nasty place

116
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:31,300
And thus it was time for the usual long battle with the dragon

117
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,700
Or at least we feared it would have been a long battle

118
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:39,366
The rail gun is overpowered and in this version the dragon is the vanilla one

119
00:06:39,866 --> 00:06:42,100
Once we took care of having a way back

120
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,933
We can go back and mind our business in pace

121
00:06:45,766 --> 00:06:51,066
And thus we are bringing back some sodalite, some celestite and some tungstate

122
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:56,133
With the ender pearls we are going to make some force field emitters

123
00:06:56,133 --> 00:07:02,966
Which can be used for a weightless armor that provides more Protection than a diamond one but at cost of energy

124
00:07:02,966 --> 00:07:06,000
And thus we can lift some weight out of our armor

125
00:07:06,933 --> 00:07:12,600
One other cool thing we can do with these things is add a plasma cannon to our hand

126
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:16,700
Anyways, to fix our portal issues and make our base work properly

127
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,300
We make a chunk loader

128
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,766
And now we can go back to our base from any place

129
00:07:22,933 --> 00:07:26,366
Now that we have secured some materials and a new room

130
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:32,566
We can move on from the machines that will use Redstone Force and start working on the GregTech ones

131
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,900
This version of GregTech actually works as an IC2 addon

132
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,966
So we have to start with a BatBox and a generator from said mod

133
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:44,800
We make a line of LV cabling and place a compressor too

134
00:07:45,133 --> 00:07:48,166
And now it is time to do some GregTech stuff

135
00:07:48,266 --> 00:07:51,133
As usual, we start from a bending machine

136
00:07:51,966 --> 00:07:55,266
And if you wonder why I didn't start from the wiremill

137
00:07:55,333 --> 00:07:57,766
It's because it requires plates

138
00:07:57,766 --> 00:08:02,400
Also, apparently, it can be made with machine hulls from any mod

139
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,333
After quickly crafting and placing it

140
00:08:05,366 --> 00:08:09,933
We can start using it and notice that it makes 3 wires from an ingot

141
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,000
Then comes the assembler

142
00:08:12,466 --> 00:08:15,600
Which for the moment we are not going to use

143
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:22,066
Since the minium stones trades makes the crafting table circuit recipe cheaper than the assembler one

144
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:25,833
Next we make a centrifuge for cheaper rubber

145
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:29,666
And to start working our ores, an electrolyzer

146
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:32,366
However that requires MV power

147
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,166
But since we can tier skip

148
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:37,166
We rush an HV battery, the MFSU

149
00:08:37,466 --> 00:08:42,866
But now our puny coal generator can barely make the power level of our battery tick up

150
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:46,100
So we make a couple of Thermal generators

151
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,933
And a setup to pump some lava from the nether

152
00:08:48,933 --> 00:08:52,833
Which we bring to our new generators using a good old tesseract

153
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:55,133
Which doesn't even require power to work

154
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:59,866
And thus we should have increased our power generation by a factor of five

155
00:09:00,733 --> 00:09:07,533
Thus we should have enough power to afford making an energy bridge to convert IC2 power into BuildCraft power

156
00:09:07,966 --> 00:09:12,133
And so we can finally have a proper power source for our RF machines

157
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:15,400
Which are still useful for a handful of tasks

158
00:09:16,166 --> 00:09:19,100
Now we can go back to our first MV machine

159
00:09:19,266 --> 00:09:20,533
The electrolyzer

160
00:09:20,533 --> 00:09:24,666
We shall use that to get stuff like aluminum out of sodalite

161
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:32,700
But the most important thing we need to electrolyze is bauxite

162
00:09:32,866 --> 00:09:36,400
Which will give us not rutile but straight up titanium dust

163
00:09:37,166 --> 00:09:41,566
And of course, to cook that stuff we need an EBF

164
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,733
Which we swiftly craft

165
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:48,166
And that machine was a power (hog?) multiblock even back in these days

166
00:09:48,966 --> 00:09:52,300
We can see the structure guideline inside the UI

167
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:55,733
After crafting and quickly building its structure

168
00:09:55,900 --> 00:10:00,166
We realize that in this version, there is no muffler hatch

169
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:03,100
So after closing off the top

170
00:10:03,166 --> 00:10:05,133
We see that the light turns green

171
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:09,000
And we have a heat capacity of 1,020 Kelvin

172
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:12,000
Which is not enough for smelting titanium

173
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:13,966
And for some reason

174
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:17,266
Aluminum here has an even higher working temperature

175
00:10:17,766 --> 00:10:19,333
If we look at the UI

176
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,766
We see two red dots in the structure

177
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:27,100
That is because we can increase the furnace temperature by adding some lava inside it

178
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:29,333
So we grab two buckets

179
00:10:29,533 --> 00:10:31,833
Take some lava out of our generators

180
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:35,066
And proceed into dropping it inside the blast furnace

181
00:10:35,466 --> 00:10:39,733
And thus we reached 1,520 Kelvin

182
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,500
Enough for titanium but not for aluminum

183
00:10:42,866 --> 00:10:46,900
So, let's fire up our electric lava furnace with titanium

184
00:10:47,333 --> 00:10:48,966
After a long cooking time

185
00:10:49,066 --> 00:10:50,100
We got two ingots

186
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,666
Which we turn into plates

187
00:10:51,666 --> 00:10:53,400
And use to make a rock cutter

188
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:58,800
Which is a power tool that will acquire Silk Touch 3 once fully charged up

189
00:10:59,066 --> 00:11:03,733
We can use that to gently take minerals out of the rock without damaging them

190
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:09,500
So that we can then throw these inside an industrial grinder to get more dust out of our ores

191
00:11:10,133 --> 00:11:11,800
Going back to our EBF

192
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:14,666
We would also like to manage to cook aluminum

193
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,500
To increase our heat capacity

194
00:11:16,766 --> 00:11:18,666
We first make some steel

195
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:21,966
Which we use to make some reinforced casings

196
00:11:22,866 --> 00:11:26,000
Each one will increase the temperature by 20 Kelvin

197
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,100
And we can even mix the blocks

198
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:30,666
We place them in a familiar way

199
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:33,600
Until we reach 2,000 Kelvin

200
00:11:33,933 --> 00:11:36,400
However, to smelt late-game materials

201
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:38,566
We need to reach 3,000

202
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:44,000
We could rebuild the whole structure with the expensive advanced machine casings

203
00:11:44,366 --> 00:11:47,066
But instead we are going to make a bunch of coils

204
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:51,266
To make these, we start off by cooking some aluminum

205
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,666
Since we now are able to do so

206
00:11:53,866 --> 00:11:55,266
While the aluminum cook

207
00:11:55,333 --> 00:11:57,733
We grind down some rubies into dust

208
00:11:58,266 --> 00:12:01,200
And then we electrolyze some chromium out of them

209
00:12:01,466 --> 00:12:04,533
Which we shall cook as soon as the aluminum is done

210
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,533
Once everything is ready

211
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,466
We rush to the rolling machine

212
00:12:08,466 --> 00:12:10,333
Where we assemble the new coils

213
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:11,733
To apply them

214
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:13,566
We simply click on the controller

215
00:12:13,666 --> 00:12:17,000
And finally we reach the temperature required for Tungsten

216
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,733
But as you probably are thinking

217
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:24,433
You can't say tungsten EBF without running out of power

218
00:12:24,433 --> 00:12:27,466
So, it is time to increase our power production

219
00:12:28,266 --> 00:12:31,533
The first upgrade we shall do is a gas turbine

220
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:37,533
So that we can recycle the methane and hydrogen made as by product of various processes

221
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:40,100
Next, to have some perpetual generation

222
00:12:40,266 --> 00:12:43,300
We make an automated farm with factorization

223
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
We are going to use a Sawmill to get the most out of the wood

224
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,533
And we also work the sawdust into charcoal for extra fuel generation

225
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:56,733
Then we burn all that fuel into a classical RailCraft boiler to make steam

226
00:12:57,666 --> 00:13:00,566
Once it heated up and started producing steam

227
00:13:00,733 --> 00:13:03,733
We feed that into a steam consumer of an energy bridge

228
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:08,266
Which will then feed power to the farm and send the leftover to our base

229
00:13:09,366 --> 00:13:12,366
This system also makes some sludgy fluid

230
00:13:12,533 --> 00:13:17,366
Which we pipe into a sludgy boiler that will send back to use some extra goodies

231
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:20,533
However, after some time

232
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:24,700
We realize that our farm outproduces the boiler consumption

233
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,366
So we increase the size of our boiler

234
00:13:27,866 --> 00:13:30,533
Once this big boy starts producing energy

235
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:35,700
We realize that we have a surplus production even while using the blast furnace

236
00:13:35,866 --> 00:13:38,866
So we start looking for a good use for that extra power

237
00:13:39,566 --> 00:13:41,466
We shall make a mass fabricator

238
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,333
Which is going to take quite a few crafting steps

239
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:49,366
And the only thing preventing us from making it is the Lapotron energy orb

240
00:13:49,366 --> 00:13:51,300
Or better, the iridium plate

241
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:56,266
We are going to need an implosion compressor and also some iridium

242
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:58,333
I haven't found any iridium ore

243
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:01,500
And I don't remember if it even spawns in this version

244
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,666
To get it we have two other options

245
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,933
Both of which include platinum

246
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:13,000
And we can get half a iridium ingot from each sheldonite ore if we work it with mercury in an industrial grinder

247
00:14:13,466 --> 00:14:16,466
Sheldonite is a quite memetic ore found in the end

248
00:14:17,133 --> 00:14:19,133
If we want to gather a proper amount

249
00:14:19,466 --> 00:14:22,166
We should go off to the small floating islands

250
00:14:22,933 --> 00:14:26,533
However, our current way of flying isn't good enough for that

251
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:30,133
Instead, we shall gather some ender pearls

252
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:35,533
So that we can craft some thrusters that we can attach to our armor for a proper jetpack flight

253
00:14:36,366 --> 00:14:39,400
Once we have properly attached and configured the jetpack

254
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,166
We can rush back to the end

255
00:14:41,166 --> 00:14:44,600
And finally fly towards the small floating islands

256
00:14:44,866 --> 00:14:47,200
Wherewith the needed materials await us

257
00:14:48,066 --> 00:14:50,866
And now that we have all the required materials

258
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,300
It is time for a crafting sequence

259
00:16:59,366 --> 00:17:01,466
Now that we have managed to craft it

260
00:17:01,466 --> 00:17:03,966
We can place it in the middle of the machine room

261
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,566
And since we want to keep some energy stocked up

262
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,900
We use an EU splitter cable to toggle it on and off

263
00:17:11,366 --> 00:17:12,200
Other than energy

264
00:17:12,666 --> 00:17:13,800
Scraps are mandatory

265
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:16,466
But we can use any material dust in place

266
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:18,900
For now we shall use thorium

267
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:23,533
And that machine uses a lot of power to produce nothing

268
00:17:23,533 --> 00:17:26,966
So, now we can try to find better ways of making power

269
00:17:27,166 --> 00:17:30,300
We start by using the surplus wood from our farm

270
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,866
And with two boiler

271
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,300
We still have excess fuel production and almost make a full HV amp

272
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:38,100
But that is still nothing

273
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,200
Since that machine can take many amps of IV power

274
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:43,366
If we want to properly feed it

275
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,700
We are going to need a fusion reactor

276
00:17:46,266 --> 00:17:51,566
However that is a complex machine to make with many steps that require a lot of materials

277
00:17:52,266 --> 00:17:55,333
We do not have AE2 to help us with that

278
00:17:55,466 --> 00:17:58,266
But we have its precursors AE1

279
00:17:58,933 --> 00:18:02,966
We start by making some cabling and some logistic processors

280
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:05,566
I mean basic processors

281
00:18:05,933 --> 00:18:08,666
Then we make a ME drive with some cells

282
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:12,300
Instead of having formation and annihilation cores

283
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,766
We have a single conversion matrix

284
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:18,133
Which we use for our first crafting terminal

285
00:18:18,133 --> 00:18:21,300
Finally, we make some engineering processors

286
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:24,733
Here called advanced processors to make a controller

287
00:18:24,733 --> 00:18:27,333
Which actually works as an energy acceptor

288
00:18:27,666 --> 00:18:33,066
We start building our AE1 system by dropping down the controller and giving it power

289
00:18:33,566 --> 00:18:36,800
Then we add our disk drive with all the cells we made

290
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,966
And to interact with it

291
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,933
We add our crafting terminal

292
00:18:41,333 --> 00:18:44,000
Now we can drop in all the items we have

293
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,366
Now, to do auto crafting

294
00:18:46,533 --> 00:18:49,366
We need a couple of interfaces and a CPU

295
00:18:49,533 --> 00:18:53,400
And here the CPU is a multiblock with a variable structure

296
00:18:53,566 --> 00:18:56,266
We shall start by making the smallest one

297
00:18:56,366 --> 00:18:59,766
Bigger ones can carry more patterns or craft faster

298
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,600
But this is actually a molecular assembler with embedded interface

299
00:19:04,133 --> 00:19:06,766
To make patterns we need an encoder

300
00:19:06,766 --> 00:19:10,066
And, of course some patterns to encode

301
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:15,600
As usual, the first patterns we shall prepare are the conversion matrix and the interface

302
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,766
So that we can expand our system

303
00:19:18,266 --> 00:19:20,700
Since these are crafting table recipes

304
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:23,766
We drop them by the giant molecular assembler

305
00:19:24,133 --> 00:19:26,300
And now time to test out if it works

306
00:19:26,766 --> 00:19:29,900
Looks like it works faster than newer versions too

307
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:33,066
Now time to encode some assembler recipes

308
00:19:33,366 --> 00:19:34,733
As we should have expected

309
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,133
We can't drag stuff from NEI

310
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:40,566
So, as in the annoying not too good days

311
00:19:40,933 --> 00:19:44,100
We have to manually craft the first item each time

312
00:19:44,566 --> 00:19:47,100
Now that we have all the inputs and outputs

313
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:49,066
We can encode the pattern

314
00:19:49,333 --> 00:19:53,333
We place it in an interface on assembler's setup and try to run it

315
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,000
And it almost worked

316
00:19:55,333 --> 00:19:57,466
Just need to click one more button

317
00:19:57,733 --> 00:19:59,733
Now that we have fixed the inputs

318
00:19:59,933 --> 00:20:02,733
We have to wait 2 minutes to test the output

319
00:20:02,966 --> 00:20:06,900
And I can't manage to make the assembler output to the interface

320
00:20:07,133 --> 00:20:09,733
An import bus is kinda of expensive

321
00:20:09,933 --> 00:20:12,066
So we go with a more brutal approach

322
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:17,833
But for some reason, I couldn't manage to make even that approach work

323
00:20:17,833 --> 00:20:24,466
Also, the way lack of crafting materials and crafting monitoring works isn't as good as in newer versions

324
00:20:24,966 --> 00:20:30,866
So I think we should go back to using chests and math like Chad artisans did in the good old times

325
00:20:31,766 --> 00:20:33,933
Going back to our fusion reactor

326
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:36,466
We shall start from making the controller

327
00:20:36,566 --> 00:20:37,766
It has many steps

328
00:20:38,133 --> 00:20:41,400
And we should start by gathering some more emeralds

329
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,400
We can get them from this NPC vendor

330
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:48,000
Which we totally did not kidnap from the isekai village

331
00:20:48,666 --> 00:20:51,133
And to gather some wool to trade with him

332
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:57,500
We spend a lot of time with some wheat in our hands to lure some sheep into walking miles to get in our herd

333
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:00,000
However, after all of that work

334
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:04,166
The vendor now refuses to buy the wool we had to work hard to

335
00:21:04,166 --> 00:21:07,933
So it is time to send him back home using alien technology

336
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,933
Going back to our project

337
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,566
Instead of emeralds

338
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,366
We shall use the olivine we gathered in the end

339
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:16,466
And once we have all the parts

340
00:21:16,866 --> 00:21:19,100
We can make the two computer cubes

341
00:21:19,533 --> 00:21:21,566
These are not just crafting parts

342
00:21:21,666 --> 00:21:24,333
But can be placed and used in various ways

343
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:28,666
For example to simulate an IC2 fusion reactor

344
00:21:28,666 --> 00:21:32,666
Which we are not making because it's not as cool as a pink donut

345
00:21:32,866 --> 00:21:34,066
So we take it back

346
00:21:34,066 --> 00:21:41,300
And remember that in this version like IC2, GregTech machines have a chance of breaking when being removed

347
00:21:41,933 --> 00:21:46,500
And while on a mining trip while waiting for the parts to make a new one

348
00:21:46,566 --> 00:21:48,533
We have found the rare iridium ore

349
00:21:49,066 --> 00:21:50,333
Which looks like a leaner

350
00:21:50,333 --> 00:21:52,933
And I'm not sure if a rock cutter can take it

351
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:55,866
So we shall take it with our bare hands

352
00:21:56,733 --> 00:22:00,800
And here we have one of the many pieces of iridium that we are going to need

353
00:22:01,166 --> 00:22:03,500
We can also use an IC2 miner

354
00:22:03,566 --> 00:22:06,466
But these things pick up more trash than materials

355
00:22:07,266 --> 00:22:09,100
Going back to our little project

356
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:11,100
We now have the second computer

357
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:15,133
And we shall move on into working at the first of the 32 coils

358
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,000
This requires some nasty stuff

359
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:21,300
But I think the worst one is the iridium reflector

360
00:22:21,566 --> 00:22:27,366
This will make each coil cost go up by one iridium plate and eight beryllium cells

361
00:22:27,766 --> 00:22:30,633
Not to mention the 32 dense copper plates

362
00:22:30,633 --> 00:22:33,233
Totalling 4 stacks of copper per coil

363
00:22:33,766 --> 00:22:37,200
To have some extra copper we can centrifuge lava

364
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:40,600
Which can also be made out of nothing with a lava fabricator

365
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:47,066
For the moment, we are going to rebuild and repurpose our nether pump and start centrifuging that

366
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:49,400
While we build up extra copper

367
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:52,133
We can go back and check how to make beryllium

368
00:22:52,533 --> 00:22:57,466
Apparently, it can only be made by electrolyzing ender pearls or emeralds

369
00:22:58,066 --> 00:23:02,133
I think the most automatable ways has to be using portal mechanics

370
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:06,566
On a second thought, that is not automatable and neither fun

371
00:23:07,066 --> 00:23:10,466
So we move on to the next step, using a grinder

372
00:23:10,766 --> 00:23:12,100
Once we set it up

373
00:23:12,133 --> 00:23:16,166
We have to trigger some endermen and bait them to teleport into its range

374
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:20,200
And then we just watch it doing its things from the high of the sky

375
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:23,933
That setup will also produce some monster essence

376
00:23:24,166 --> 00:23:26,666
Which we can teleport back to our base

377
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:32,133
Where we may use that essence to power a mob farm to produce even more pearls

378
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:34,466
Look at how they drop fast

379
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:37,200
Once we have some to start working with

380
00:23:37,266 --> 00:23:40,766
We can proceed into pulverizing and electrifying these

381
00:23:41,266 --> 00:23:43,400
And thus we finally have the beryllium

382
00:23:43,866 --> 00:23:47,500
We also get some nitrogen and potassium as by product

383
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:52,766
Which can be used to make gunpowder for the explosives to compress the iridium plates

384
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:56,533
Finally, we compress a lot of copper

385
00:23:56,666 --> 00:24:03,300
So that we can fill our inventory with neutron reflector that we combine into the iridium neutron reflector

386
00:24:03,366 --> 00:24:06,366
The only thing left to make is the superconductor

387
00:24:06,466 --> 00:24:09,633
Which will need one more iridium plate

388
00:24:09,633 --> 00:24:13,566
So, while our assemblers are working on the energy flow circuits

389
00:24:13,733 --> 00:24:16,533
We head back to the end to mine more sheldonite

390
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,933
While there, we can also gather some sodalite

391
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:23,200
Which can be electrolyzed to obtain some sodium

392
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,733
And we use that for making sodium-potassium coolant cells

393
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,700
Now that we have everything

394
00:24:29,966 --> 00:24:31,800
We can finish our superconductor

395
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:34,666
And then complete the first fusion coil

396
00:24:34,666 --> 00:24:41,533
Finally, we can appreciate the crafting process of the fusion control computer without any video speed up

397
00:24:41,766 --> 00:24:44,933
To get started we prepare a donut of dirt

398
00:24:44,933 --> 00:24:50,100
And place the computer as the first final block that touches the ring in the inner side

399
00:24:50,566 --> 00:24:52,666
Now we have to craft a lot of stuff

400
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:54,800
And we shall start from the coils

401
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:59,800
To do that, the first step shall be to step on our charge pad

402
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:02,900
So that we keep our armor charged while being AFK

403
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,466
After being AFK for some time

404
00:25:05,666 --> 00:25:09,333
Our centrifuges managed to make some copper and electrum

405
00:25:09,366 --> 00:25:11,366
Which are fundamental for the coils

406
00:25:12,166 --> 00:25:16,100
Now, the copper will be required for all the neutron reflectors

407
00:25:16,466 --> 00:25:19,666
And the electrum will greatly cut the cost of the circuits

408
00:25:20,066 --> 00:25:24,100
But the main issue is going to be the highly advanced machine block

409
00:25:24,533 --> 00:25:27,866
We need 2 stacks of titanium and 2 of chromium

410
00:25:28,266 --> 00:25:32,166
Titanium could be made by staying AFK to stock up UU-matter

411
00:25:32,366 --> 00:25:35,166
But chromium can only be made by rubies

412
00:25:35,566 --> 00:25:38,600
And that would make us have to dig 7 stacks of them

413
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,666
Which is not going to happen

414
00:25:41,133 --> 00:25:44,166
The IC2 mine doesn't seem to work properly

415
00:25:44,366 --> 00:25:47,466
So we shall take its drill and upgrade it to a quarry

416
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:53,700
And we can get some extra diamonds by compressing all the junk that came out of the sludge of our farm

417
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,933
On diamond you can't grow flowers

418
00:25:56,466 --> 00:26:03,300
But you can use sludge to make diamonds that can craft a quarry that will gather every useful resource you could possibly need

419
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:07,866
We place it with some tesseract to manage its input and outputs

420
00:26:08,166 --> 00:26:11,000
Then we can watch its robot build the structure

421
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:13,166
Once the frame is complete

422
00:26:13,400 --> 00:26:17,466
The head will start running with all the power of about one blast furnace

423
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,900
On the other side of the tesseract

424
00:26:20,066 --> 00:26:23,266
We are managing the output in the worst possible way

425
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:26,200
Since I can't find any better compatible pipe

426
00:26:26,666 --> 00:26:27,700
After some time

427
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:31,500
We have managed to fill one super chest of cobblestone

428
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:35,200
And we can see about what we are going to get from our quarry

429
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:38,533
So, we can move our tesseract to a better sorting facility

430
00:26:39,266 --> 00:26:45,600
We shall stock inside some barrels all of the garbage from decorative mods that can cause visual glitches and lag

431
00:26:45,733 --> 00:26:48,366
While we keep the good stuff inside this chest

432
00:26:49,166 --> 00:26:52,800
Then, since we are going to have a lot of extra quartz

433
00:26:52,966 --> 00:26:58,300
We can use that to make input buses and other AE1 stuff to automate the processing

434
00:26:58,766 --> 00:27:05,866
And we shall invest two coils worth of machine hulls in a quantum chest to see how much cobblestone we dig

435
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:09,400
So, time to start using all of that goodies

436
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:13,266
We shall also improve our workshop to be more automatic

437
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,100
However, it looks like back in the day

438
00:27:16,366 --> 00:27:19,366
Artisans used to make good stuff by hand

439
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:22,300
And not with ugly automated setups

440
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:28,200
You can tell by the lack of vanilla hoppers and how hard it is to get stuff out of chests and machines

441
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:31,100
And after many tries

442
00:27:31,266 --> 00:27:34,966
I gave up upon trying to get plates out of a bending machine

443
00:27:35,366 --> 00:27:39,300
It have has something that looks like the newer auto output function

444
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,933
But I'm too clumsy to make it work

445
00:27:42,766 --> 00:27:45,066
Anyways, we make a second grinder

446
00:27:45,066 --> 00:27:47,266
And we wall share it with the older one

447
00:27:47,466 --> 00:27:51,566
And stock it up with some water using the worst pipes we could find

448
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:54,333
Next we also make an electrolyzer

449
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:59,333
And now we make AE1 craft some input and export buses

450
00:27:59,966 --> 00:28:02,600
Automating Thermal expansion is rather easy

451
00:28:02,766 --> 00:28:08,400
But these old rusty GregTech machines require us to find the correct side for each input

452
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:13,766
And with that we have automated almost everything like a good (virgin?) engineer should do

453
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:17,266
The only problematic thing left to manage is Iridium

454
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:22,000
The only way I know of getting it in good amounts is with UU matter

455
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:27,766
However, we managed to make only 3 pieces since when we built the matter fabricator

456
00:28:27,766 --> 00:28:30,666
So, maybe we could do a fusion reactor for the moment

457
00:28:31,266 --> 00:28:33,700
Or we could make one ultimate solar panel

458
00:28:33,700 --> 00:28:37,133
Which will give a longer use to the uranium we aren't using

459
00:28:37,533 --> 00:28:38,600
Or maybe not

460
00:28:38,866 --> 00:28:42,466
Since that requires half fusion reactor worth of iridium

461
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:46,100
Now a vacuum reactor would make quite some power

462
00:28:46,766 --> 00:28:51,800
However, the vacuum freezer would use all that power to cool down the coolant cells

463
00:28:52,333 --> 00:28:54,900
So we have to move on to something more efficient

464
00:28:55,266 --> 00:28:58,166
And there we have a quick and dirty plutonium reactor

465
00:28:58,166 --> 00:29:01,566
Which makes about as much power as two railcraft boilers

466
00:29:02,100 --> 00:29:05,966
We won't use the quad cells because these take too much copper

467
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:08,566
And once our quarry runs out

468
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:12,500
We make one more so that it won't be alone in his next location

469
00:29:13,066 --> 00:29:14,000
Double the quarry

470
00:29:14,266 --> 00:29:15,066
Double the fun

471
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:18,966
And now time to AFK while we stock up resources

472
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:20,600
Once we have enough

473
00:29:20,700 --> 00:29:24,500
We can start improving our base with the following automation sequence

474
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:52,900
Once we complete the donut

475
00:33:52,900 --> 00:33:55,333
We add two input material injectors

476
00:33:55,666 --> 00:33:58,533
One material injector and four energy injectors

477
00:33:59,466 --> 00:34:04,533
Which have the same location of the GTNH fusion reactors

478
00:34:04,533 --> 00:34:09,433
Next, we connect the power and we wait for the reactor internal buffer to charge up

479
00:34:09,433 --> 00:34:13,333
With our current production, that will take about a quarter of an hour

480
00:34:14,166 --> 00:34:15,000
While we wait

481
00:34:15,266 --> 00:34:16,733
Let's prepare the fuel

482
00:34:16,766 --> 00:34:20,266
We start by electrolyzing some hydrogen out of water

483
00:34:21,066 --> 00:34:24,100
Next we centrifuge some deuterium out of that

484
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:27,733
Finally, we make some tritium out of deuterium

485
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:31,700
Now, when we will fuse deuterium and tritium

486
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:34,866
We are going to get some helium plasma

487
00:34:34,866 --> 00:34:38,300
Which, to be used, requires a plasma generator

488
00:34:38,966 --> 00:34:42,266
That machine contains some tungsten steel

489
00:34:42,266 --> 00:34:47,066
Which, as the tooltip says, has to be vacuum hardened

490
00:34:47,066 --> 00:34:49,533
So, while our tungsten steel is cooking

491
00:34:49,666 --> 00:34:52,166
We shall work on a vacuum freezer

492
00:34:52,966 --> 00:34:56,133
And as expected, that is a multiblock machine

493
00:34:57,133 --> 00:34:59,566
But it's always the same machine hulls

494
00:34:59,566 --> 00:35:01,800
And we quickly complete it

495
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:05,966
Meanwhile, our fusion reactor reached one quarter of the charge

496
00:35:06,666 --> 00:35:09,166
But that might be the maximum of our reactor

497
00:35:09,333 --> 00:35:13,400
Since we only have four of the 16 maximum energy injectors

498
00:35:14,533 --> 00:35:18,600
So let's try giving it some fuel and let's see if it works

499
00:35:19,266 --> 00:35:21,000
The lights did not turn on

500
00:35:21,100 --> 00:35:23,366
But we lost all of our stored energy

501
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:27,400
But it looks like we managed to get one cell of plasma

502
00:35:27,666 --> 00:35:29,466
To keep a sustained fusion

503
00:35:29,500 --> 00:35:31,866
We craft one more energy injector

504
00:35:32,166 --> 00:35:33,900
And attach it to the coils

505
00:35:34,333 --> 00:35:36,533
After buffering up enough power again

506
00:35:36,666 --> 00:35:38,000
We drop in the fuel

507
00:35:38,533 --> 00:35:40,866
And this time the lights turned on

508
00:35:40,866 --> 00:35:44,600
And we are producing a constant flux of helium plasma

509
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:46,366
Other than the hot plasma

510
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,566
We also have hot tungsten steel

511
00:35:48,733 --> 00:35:52,366
And only one of the two shall go inside the vacuum freezer

512
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,800
And thus we have our plasma generator

513
00:35:54,800 --> 00:35:57,933
Which we shall place right next to the matter fabricator

514
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,766
Finally, we feed it some plasma

515
00:36:00,766 --> 00:36:03,800
So that we can finally have a proper UU matter production

516
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:09,600
Our matter fabricator is indeed receiving so much power that it can't even work that fast

517
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,966
And its energy buffer is filling up

518
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,966
And as you probably noticed

519
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:17,733
That's not just the power of one plasma generator

520
00:36:18,100 --> 00:36:21,133
It's also the power of the new generators on the wall

521
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:27,566
The only thing left to do is to show off our cobblestone collection in our AE1 system

522
00:36:27,966 --> 00:36:29,566
So we make a storage bus

523
00:36:29,566 --> 00:36:31,400
And connect it to the quantum Chest

524
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,333
员工们好

525
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:06,066
今天我们要再玩一个又老又好的整合包 FTB Ultimate

526
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,500
这也是我第一次遇到 GregTech 这个 mod 的整合包

527
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:14,966
总之 我们快速新建一个新世界

528
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,900
我们出生在一个村庄附近 不过这个村庄似乎没有任何战利品箱

529
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,333
快速瞄了一眼之后

530
00:00:22,366 --> 00:00:25,300
我们开始做原版的生存流程

531
00:00:25,866 --> 00:00:28,966
也就是速速做一张床然后收集一些材料

532
00:00:29,466 --> 00:00:31,666
既然我们有了床和一些食物

533
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:33,800
可以去采集一些矿物了

534
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,066
这些应该足够让我们的基地启动了

535
00:00:54,466 --> 00:00:58,066
我们要做的第一件事是搞点建筑材料

536
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,266
我们打算用经典可靠的石砖来建造基地

537
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,966
经过一番工作之后

538
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:07,666
这就是我们的新基地了 顶上有一扇漂亮的天窗

539
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:12,133
现在我们可以开始用老版本的粉碎机来处理矿物了

540
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,400
这是在 Forge Energy （FE）单位出现之前的版本

541
00:01:15,666 --> 00:01:18,166
我们曾经用的是 Minecraft Joules（MJ）

542
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:21,266
好 在继续建设我们的工厂之前

543
00:01:21,366 --> 00:01:23,200
我们先去搞点像样的工具

544
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:24,900
比如动力装甲

545
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,666
这个版本的装甲看起来好挫

546
00:01:27,766 --> 00:01:29,566
我们刚做这个装甲出来的时候

547
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,066
它只会让我们外观看上去不一样而已

548
00:01:32,166 --> 00:01:33,933
要让它真正有用

549
00:01:34,066 --> 00:01:36,166
我们需要一个动力装甲改装台

550
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:40,266
它需要一颗绿宝石 而我们挖矿的时候并没有找到

551
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,733
不过幸运的是 这个版本有村民交易

552
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:45,800
那个村民的出价很不错

553
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,500
我们从公会大厅接下了这个任务

554
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,333
然后迅速完成它

555
00:01:50,566 --> 00:01:53,700
这样我们就有了改装台来调整我们的装甲

556
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,900
在里面可以看到装甲已装备的模块

557
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,300
我们可以添加、移除或编辑它们

558
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:04,300
我们首先想要的是加一些装甲板 这样就能提供一定的防护

559
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,800
我们快速合成了升级所需的材料

560
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,500
然后安装到我们的装甲上

561
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:14,466
接下来 我们可以选择装甲板有多厚

562
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,000
越厚 我们获得的护甲就越多

563
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:20,133
但我们也需要承担更多的重量

564
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,500
既然我们想保护做到位

565
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:26,566
我们在装甲的每一件上都装了最厚的那一档

566
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:31,300
于是我们就拥有了一件不损坏 和钻石甲一样好但用的只是铁做成的装甲

567
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,066
问题是它很重

568
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,733
为了解决这个问题

569
00:02:34,866 --> 00:02:40,466
我们可以在护腿上安装一些增强模块来帮助我们在负重状态下行走

570
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:46,833
同样 我们可以调整这些增强模块的功率大小和它们帮助我们行走的方式

571
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,733
然而 这些都需要电力

572
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,600
所以我们还必须安装电池

573
00:02:51,966 --> 00:02:54,500
这会让我们的重量进一步增加

574
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,666
当然 我们还需要一些发电机来给电池充电

575
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:05,100
然而 所有可以嵌入装甲的发电机都需要控制电路

576
00:03:05,366 --> 00:03:06,800
而控制电路需要荧石

577
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,700
在去下界之前

578
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:10,366
我们先合成一个电动工具

579
00:03:10,566 --> 00:03:12,700
其他所有工具都可以不用了

580
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,666
释放大量快捷栏空间

581
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:18,933
这个机械臂非常万能

582
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,400
比如作为基本的挖矿工具

583
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,266
为了挖掘黑曜石

584
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,533
我们可以用一些钻石来升级它

585
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:30,466
而且我们可能需要把镐子功能超频到最大来完成这个任务

586
00:03:30,466 --> 00:03:34,800
这样我们就可以用我们的机器手来挖掘黑曜石了

587
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:39,266
在进入下界之前 我们还应该搞一些更酷的功能

588
00:03:39,266 --> 00:03:40,333
比如轨道炮

589
00:03:40,666 --> 00:03:42,900
或者我们可以晚点再做

590
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,266
目前先搞一个近战助手应该就够了

591
00:03:46,666 --> 00:03:50,166
然后我们用 IC2 发电机给装甲充满电

592
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,966
一旦我们充满电并装备齐全

593
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,333
我们开始另一趟远征

594
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,800
这趟的唯一目标是收集一些荧石粉

595
00:04:00,733 --> 00:04:03,866
我们迅速完成任务然后回家

596
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:05,533
带着这些匆忙收集的战利品

597
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,500
我们终于可以做几个高压电容器了

598
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:12,133
这样我们就可以在机械手上安装轨道炮了

599
00:04:12,533 --> 00:04:13,933
当然

600
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,100
我们把它按到最大功率

601
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,100
轨道炮有两个主要用途

602
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,933
一个是作为远程武器使用

603
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,566
但最重要的那个

604
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:28,666
是我们可以利用它的后坐力飞来飞去

605
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
于是我们能很快就找到一片沙漠

606
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,800
在那里我们可以获得控制电路所需缺少的另一种材料——仙人掌

607
00:04:37,266 --> 00:04:40,500
有了它 我们就可以在头盔上装一个太阳能发电机了

608
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:44,000
我们还可以搞到夜视镜

609
00:04:44,866 --> 00:04:48,166
然后是自动喂食器 这样我们就不用管食物了

610
00:04:48,966 --> 00:04:51,733
还有我们潜水时用的电解器

611
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:56,000
但真正夯的是搞一个动能发电机

612
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,500
这个模块会在我们走路的时候产生能量

613
00:04:58,566 --> 00:05:00,600
但它会让行走变得更困难

614
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:04,700
然而 它产生的能量比外骨骼辅助消耗的还要多

615
00:05:05,866 --> 00:05:07,333
但这是个科技整合包

616
00:05:07,466 --> 00:05:09,300
所以别再摸鱼了

617
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:13,466
我们得多做一些老版本的热力膨胀机器

618
00:05:14,666 --> 00:05:17,666
然后用它们来扩建我们的基地

619
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:22,666
因为 GregTech 的那些真正的机器需要更多空间

620
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:26,133
在我们等待建筑材料的时候

621
00:05:26,366 --> 00:05:28,800
我们可以再多收集一些资源

622
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:33,500
不过看起来基础处理工序还需要花不少时间

623
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:40,100
所以我们就利用这段时间去末地多收集一些末影珍珠 用来做更多装甲升级

624
00:05:40,566 --> 00:05:42,533
在去末地的路上

625
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:44,133
我们发现了一个地牢

626
00:05:44,533 --> 00:05:46,266
在探索地牢的时候

627
00:05:46,466 --> 00:05:48,300
我们找到了另一个有趣的玩具

628
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:49,333
一把传送枪

629
00:05:49,966 --> 00:05:52,400
这是又一个伟大游戏的美好回忆

630
00:05:52,566 --> 00:05:54,266
如果你不知这个枪什么用的话

631
00:05:54,333 --> 00:05:59,400
这个物品可以让我们在墙上创建传送门 这样我们就能轻松地传送

632
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:03,766
它还可以用来移动任何生物或物品

633
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:10,500
没错 它最夯的用法是在多人服务器上整蛊别人

634
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,066
不管怎样 回到我们的冒险

635
00:06:13,266 --> 00:06:16,266
等我们找到并搭建好了末地传送门

636
00:06:16,366 --> 00:06:18,566
我们开始收集一些末影珍珠

637
00:06:19,166 --> 00:06:22,066
但当我们收集够了想要回去的时候

638
00:06:22,133 --> 00:06:27,166
我们发现传送枪并不能把我们带离那个糟糕的地方

639
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:31,300
于是就又到了和龙进行持久战的时候了

640
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,700
或者说至少我们以为是一场持久恶战

641
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:39,366
这个版本轨道炮实在太强了 而且这个版本的龙是原版的

642
00:06:39,866 --> 00:06:42,100
等我们搞定了回家的路

643
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,933
就可以回去安心忙我们的事了

644
00:06:45,766 --> 00:06:51,066
于是我们带回了一些方钠石、天青石以及一些钨酸锂

645
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:56,133
我们用末影珍珠做一些力场发射器

646
00:06:56,133 --> 00:07:02,966
它可以用来做没有重量的装甲 护甲比钻石甲更高 但消耗能量

647
00:07:02,966 --> 00:07:06,000
这样我们就能让装甲减重了

648
00:07:06,933 --> 00:07:12,600
这些东西还能做的另一个很夯的事是在手上加一门等离子炮

649
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:16,700
不管怎样 为了解决传送门的问题并让基地正常运行

650
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,300
我们做了一个区块加载器

651
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,766
现在我们就可以从任何地方回到基地了

652
00:07:22,933 --> 00:07:26,366
现在我们弄到了一些材料和新房间

653
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:32,566
我们可以从那些使用 Redstone Force （RF）的机器中毕业 开始做 GregTech 的机器了

654
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,900
这个版本的 GregTech 实际上是 IC2 的一个附属 mod 的

655
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,966
所以我们得先做一个低压存电箱和一个那个 mod 的发电机

656
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:44,800
我们铺了一条低压线缆 又放压缩机

657
00:07:45,133 --> 00:07:48,166
现在是时候做点 GregTech 的东西了

658
00:07:48,266 --> 00:07:51,133
像往常一样 我们从卷板机开始

659
00:07:51,966 --> 00:07:55,266
如果你好奇为什么我不从线材轧机开始

660
00:07:55,333 --> 00:07:57,766
是因为线材轧机配方需要板

661
00:07:57,766 --> 00:08:02,400
另外 很显然 它可以用任何 mod 的机器外壳来制作

662
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,333
快速合成并放下之后

663
00:08:05,366 --> 00:08:09,933
我们开始使用它 发现一个锭可以做出 3 根导线

664
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,000
然后轮到了组装机

665
00:08:12,466 --> 00:08:15,600
目前我们暂且不用它

666
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:22,066
因为用贤者之石交易工作台电路比用组装机做更便宜

667
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:25,833
接下来我们做一个离心机 用来搞便宜的橡胶

668
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:29,666
然后要开始处理矿石了 做一个电解机

669
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:32,366
然而这需要 MV 电力

670
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,166
不过既然我们可以跳级

671
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:37,166
我们直接速做了一个高压电池——MFSU

672
00:08:37,466 --> 00:08:42,866
但现在我们那可怜的燃煤发电机几乎填不上电池的电量

673
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:46,100
所以我们做了几个地热发电机

674
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,933
还有一个从下界抽岩浆的装置

675
00:08:48,933 --> 00:08:52,833
我们用一个又老又好的超立方体把它输送到新发电机那里

676
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:55,133
它甚至不需要电力就能工作

677
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:59,866
这样我们的发电量应该提升了五倍

678
00:09:00,733 --> 00:09:07,533
这样我们应该有足够的电力来做一座能量转换器 把 IC2 电力转换成 BC 电力

679
00:09:07,966 --> 00:09:12,133
这样我们就终于能给我们的 RF 机器提供像样的电源了

680
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:15,400
它们在少部分任务里仍然有用

681
00:09:16,166 --> 00:09:19,100
现在我们回到第一台中压机器

682
00:09:19,266 --> 00:09:20,533
电解机

683
00:09:20,533 --> 00:09:24,666
我们会用它获得一些矿物 比如从方钠石中提取铝

684
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:32,700
但我们需要电解的最重要的东西是铝土矿

685
00:09:32,866 --> 00:09:36,400
它电解出的不是金红石 而是直接给钛粉

686
00:09:37,166 --> 00:09:41,566
当然 要烧这些东西我们需要一台电高炉

687
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,733
我们速合成出来

688
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:48,166
这台机器即使在当时也已经是一个耗电大户的多方块结构了

689
00:09:48,966 --> 00:09:52,300
我们可以在 UI 里面看到结构指南

690
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:55,733
合成并速搭好结构之后

691
00:09:55,900 --> 00:10:00,166
我们意识到这个版本里没有消声仓

692
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:03,100
所以在封上顶部之后

693
00:10:03,166 --> 00:10:05,133
我们看到指示灯变绿了

694
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:09,000
我们有了 1020K 的热容量

695
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:12,000
这还不足以熔炼钛

696
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:13,966
而且不知为什么

697
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:17,266
这个版本里铝的工作温度更高

698
00:10:17,766 --> 00:10:19,333
如果看一下界面

699
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,766
我们看到结构中有两个红点

700
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:27,100
那是因为我们可以往里面加岩浆来提高炉温

701
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:29,333
所以我们拿两桶

702
00:10:29,533 --> 00:10:31,833
从我们的发电机里取出一些岩浆

703
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:35,066
然后把它倒进高炉里

704
00:10:35,466 --> 00:10:39,733
于是我们达到了 1520K

705
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,500
足够烧钛但不够烧铝

706
00:10:42,866 --> 00:10:46,900
那么 让我们把电高炉开起来 烧钛

707
00:10:47,333 --> 00:10:48,966
经过了漫长的烧制时间之后

708
00:10:49,066 --> 00:10:50,100
我们得到了两个锭

709
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,666
把它们做成板

710
00:10:51,666 --> 00:10:53,400
然后用来做一个岩石切割机

711
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:58,800
这是一个电动工具 充满电后能获得精准采集 III

712
00:10:59,066 --> 00:11:03,733
我们可以用它来温柔地把矿石从岩石里取出来 不损坏它们

713
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:09,500
这样我们就可以把它们扔进工业研磨机里 从矿石中获得更多的粉

714
00:11:10,133 --> 00:11:11,800
回到我们的电高炉

715
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:14,666
我们还想烧铝

716
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,500
为了提升热容量

717
00:11:16,766 --> 00:11:18,666
我们先做一些钢

718
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:21,966
用它们来做一些强化外壳

719
00:11:22,866 --> 00:11:26,000
每个强化外壳能提升 20K 的温度

720
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,100
而且我们还可以混着用

721
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:30,666
我们用一种熟悉的方式摆放它们

722
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:33,600
直到我们达到 2000K

723
00:11:33,933 --> 00:11:36,400
然而 要熔炼后期材料

724
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:38,566
我们需要达到 3000K

725
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:44,000
我们可以用昂贵的进阶机器外壳重建整个结构

726
00:11:44,366 --> 00:11:47,066
但反过来 我们打算做一堆线圈

727
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:51,266
要开始做线圈 我们先烧一些铝

728
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,666
因为我们现在能烧了

729
00:11:53,866 --> 00:11:55,266
在铝烧制的过程中

730
00:11:55,333 --> 00:11:57,733
我们把一些红宝石磨成粉

731
00:11:58,266 --> 00:12:01,200
然后从里面电解出铬

732
00:12:01,466 --> 00:12:04,533
铝一烧完我们就开始烧它

733
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,533
一切都准备就绪之后

734
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,466
我们冲到辊压机那里

735
00:12:08,466 --> 00:12:10,333
在那里我们把新线圈组装起来

736
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:11,733
要安装它们

737
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:13,566
我们只需要点一下控制器

738
00:12:13,666 --> 00:12:17,000
终于我们达到了烧钨所需的温度

739
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,733
但正如你可能在想的那样

740
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:24,433
你不可能用电高炉烧钨而不把电用完

741
00:12:24,433 --> 00:12:27,466
所以 是时候提高我们的发电量了

742
00:12:28,266 --> 00:12:31,533
我们要做的第一个升级是燃气涡轮

743
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:37,533
这样我们就可以回收各种工序产生的副产：甲烷和氢气

744
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:40,100
接下来 为了保持持续的发电

745
00:12:40,266 --> 00:12:43,300
我们用因式分解做了一个自动化农场

746
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
我们打算用锯木机来最大化木材的产出

747
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,533
我们还把锯末加工成木炭 以产生更多燃料

748
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:56,733
然后我们把这些燃料全部烧进一台经典的 RC 锅炉来产生蒸汽

749
00:12:57,666 --> 00:13:00,566
等它加热并开始产生蒸汽之后

750
00:13:00,733 --> 00:13:03,733
我们把蒸汽送进能量转换器的蒸汽消耗器

751
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:08,266
然后它就会向农场供电并把其他电送回基地

752
00:13:09,366 --> 00:13:12,366
这个系统还会产生一些污泥流体

753
00:13:12,533 --> 00:13:17,366
我们把它用管道送进一个污泥锅炉 它会给我们一些额外的电量

754
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:20,533
然而 过了一段时间之后

755
00:13:20,666 --> 00:13:24,700
我们发现农场产量超出了锅炉的消耗

756
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,366
于是我们加大了锅炉的尺寸

757
00:13:27,866 --> 00:13:30,533
等这个大家伙开始产能之后

758
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:35,700
我们发现即使在用着高炉的情况下仍然有富余产量

759
00:13:35,866 --> 00:13:38,866
于是我们开始找这些多余电力的好用途

760
00:13:39,566 --> 00:13:41,466
我们将做一个物质制造机

761
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,333
这需要相当多的合成步骤

762
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:49,366
而唯一阻碍我们做出它的东西就是兰博顿能量球

763
00:13:49,366 --> 00:13:51,300
或者更准确地说 铱板

764
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:56,266
我们需要一台聚爆压缩机和一些铱

765
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:58,333
我还没有找到任何铱矿石

766
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:01,500
而且我不记得铱矿石是否在这个版本中生成

767
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,666
为了得到它 我们还有另外两种方案

768
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,933
两种方案都和铂有关

769
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:13,000
如果我们在工业研磨机中使用汞来处理谢尔顿矿石 每个可以得到半个铱锭

770
00:14:13,466 --> 00:14:16,466
谢尔顿矿可以在末地找到 一种名字很有梗的矿石

771
00:14:17,133 --> 00:14:19,133
如果我们想收集到足够的数量

772
00:14:19,466 --> 00:14:22,166
我们应该去那些小浮岛

773
00:14:22,933 --> 00:14:26,533
然而 我们目前的飞行方式还不方便

774
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:30,133
另一种方法是 我们先收集一些末影珍珠

775
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:35,533
这样我们就可以制作一些推进器 安装到装甲上 实现真正的喷气背包飞行

776
00:14:36,366 --> 00:14:39,400
等我们把喷气背包安装好并正确配置之后

777
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,166
我们可以冲回末地

778
00:14:41,166 --> 00:14:44,600
终于可以飞向那些小浮岛了

779
00:14:44,866 --> 00:14:47,200
那里有我们需要的材料在等着我们

780
00:14:48,066 --> 00:14:50,866
现在我们有了所有需要的材料

781
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,300
是时候来一段手搓纯享版了

782
00:16:59,366 --> 00:17:01,466
既然我们把它合成了出来

783
00:17:01,466 --> 00:17:03,966
我们可以把它放在工作间正中央

784
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,566
既然我们想储存一些能量

785
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,900
我们用 EU 分线线缆来控制开关

786
00:17:11,366 --> 00:17:12,200
除了能量之外

787
00:17:12,666 --> 00:17:13,800
废料是强制性的

788
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:16,466
不过我们可以用别的材料粉末来替代

789
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:18,900
现在我们先用钍

790
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:23,533
既然这台机器消耗巨量电力却什么也不产出

791
00:17:23,533 --> 00:17:26,966
那么现在我们可以尝试找更好的发电方式

792
00:17:27,166 --> 00:17:30,300
我们从利用农场多产出的木材开始

793
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,866
用上了两个锅炉

794
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,300
我们仍然燃料产量有余 产出几乎到 HV 的 1A

795
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:38,100
但这还不够

796
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,200
因为那台机器可以吃进好 IV 的好几 A

797
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:43,366
如果我们想满足它的能源需求

798
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,700
我们需要一个聚变反应堆

799
00:17:46,266 --> 00:17:51,566
然而那是一台制造过程很复杂、步骤很多、需要大量材料的机器

800
00:17:52,266 --> 00:17:55,333
我们没有 AE2 来帮我们

801
00:17:55,466 --> 00:17:58,266
但我们有它的前身 AE1

802
00:17:58,933 --> 00:18:02,966
我们先做一些线缆和一些物流处理器

803
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:05,566
我是说基础处理器

804
00:18:05,933 --> 00:18:08,666
然后我们做一个 ME 驱动器 还有一些存储元件

805
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:12,300
AE1 里没有成形核心和破坏核心

806
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,766
取而代之的是一个转换矩阵

807
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:18,133
我们用它来制作第一个合成终端

808
00:18:18,133 --> 00:18:21,300
最后 我们做一些工程处理器

809
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:24,733
在这里叫做进阶处理器 用来做一个控制器

810
00:18:24,733 --> 00:18:27,333
它的实际功能是能量接收器

811
00:18:27,666 --> 00:18:33,066
我们开始搭建 AE1 系统 放置控制器方块并给它通电

812
00:18:33,566 --> 00:18:36,800
然后我们加上磁盘驱动器以及我们做好的所有存储元件

813
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,966
要与之交互的话

814
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,933
我们加上合成终端

815
00:18:41,333 --> 00:18:44,000
现在我们可以把所有物品都丢进去了

816
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,366
现在 要做自动合成

817
00:18:46,533 --> 00:18:49,366
我们需要几个接口和一个 CPU

818
00:18:49,533 --> 00:18:53,400
在这里 CPU 是一个可变尺寸的多方块结构

819
00:18:53,566 --> 00:18:56,266
我们从做最小的结构那个开始

820
00:18:56,366 --> 00:18:59,766
更大的可以容纳更多样板或者合成得更快

821
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,600
但这其实是一个有界面的分子装配室

822
00:19:04,133 --> 00:19:06,766
要做样板的话 我们需要一个编码器

823
00:19:06,766 --> 00:19:10,066
当然 还有一些需要编码的空白样板

824
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:15,600
像往常一样 我们首先准备的样板是转换矩阵和接口

825
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,766
这样我们就可以扩展我们的系统

826
00:19:18,266 --> 00:19:20,700
由于这些是工作台配方

827
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:23,766
我们把它们放在巨大的分子装配室里

828
00:19:24,133 --> 00:19:26,300
现在是时候测试一下它是否正常工作了

829
00:19:26,766 --> 00:19:29,900
看起来它比新版本合成得还要快

830
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:33,066
现在是时候编码一些组装机配方了

831
00:19:33,366 --> 00:19:34,733
正如我们所料

832
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,133
我们不能从 NEI 拖拽物品

833
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:40,566
所以 一如当年那些又烦又不好的日子

834
00:19:40,933 --> 00:19:44,100
我们每次都必须手动合成第一个物品

835
00:19:44,566 --> 00:19:47,100
现在我们有了所有的输入和输出

836
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:49,066
我们可以编码样板了

837
00:19:49,333 --> 00:19:53,333
我们把它放在组装机配置的接口上 并尝试运行

838
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,000
它差点就成功了

839
00:19:55,333 --> 00:19:57,466
只需要点一个按钮就能修复

840
00:19:57,733 --> 00:19:59,733
现在我们修好了输入的问题

841
00:19:59,933 --> 00:20:02,733
我们必须每次等两分钟来测试输出

842
00:20:02,966 --> 00:20:06,900
而且我不能让组装机正确输出回接口

843
00:20:07,133 --> 00:20:09,733
输入总线有点贵

844
00:20:09,933 --> 00:20:12,066
所以我们采取了一个更暴力的做法

845
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:17,833
但不知为何 我连那个方法也没能让它正常输出

846
00:20:17,833 --> 00:20:24,466
另外 缺少合成材料和合成监控这一点 做得也不如后来的版本好

847
00:20:24,966 --> 00:20:30,866
所以我觉得我们应该回到用箱子和手动算材料的方式 像老资历以前那样又老又好地手搓

848
00:20:31,766 --> 00:20:33,933
回到我们的聚变反应堆

849
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:36,466
我们从制作控制器开始

850
00:20:36,566 --> 00:20:37,766
合成步骤很多

851
00:20:38,133 --> 00:20:41,400
我们应该从多收集一些绿宝石开始

852
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,400
我们可以从这个交易 NPC 那里获得

853
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:48,000
当然我们绝对没有从异世界村庄绑他回来

854
00:20:48,666 --> 00:20:51,133
为了收集羊毛来跟他交易

855
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:57,500
我们花了很多时间 拿着小麦勾引一些羊走很远的路来加入我们的羊群

856
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:00,000
然而 做完这么多工作之后

857
00:21:00,166 --> 00:21:04,166
这个 NPC 现在拒绝购买我们辛辛苦苦弄来的羊毛

858
00:21:04,166 --> 00:21:07,933
所以是时候用外星科技送他回家了

859
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,933
回到我们的目标上

860
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,566
不用绿宝石了

861
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,366
我们用之前在末地收集到的橄榄石代替

862
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:16,466
等我们有了所有合成材料之后

863
00:21:16,866 --> 00:21:19,100
我们可以做出两个计算机立方体

864
00:21:19,533 --> 00:21:21,566
这些不仅仅是合成材料

865
00:21:21,666 --> 00:21:24,333
还可以放置下来 有不少功能

866
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:28,666
例如模拟一个 IC2 聚变反应堆

867
00:21:28,666 --> 00:21:32,666
我们不打算做那个 因为它没有粉色甜甜圈那么有逼格

868
00:21:32,866 --> 00:21:34,066
所以我们把它取回来

869
00:21:34,066 --> 00:21:41,300
然后想起来了 和 IC2 一样 这个版本里 GregTech 机器在拆除时有几率损坏

870
00:21:41,933 --> 00:21:46,500
在挖矿的过程中 一边等零件做一个新的

871
00:21:46,566 --> 00:21:48,533
我们找到了罕见的铱矿石

872
00:21:49,066 --> 00:21:50,333
它似乎在地层里相当贫瘠

873
00:21:50,333 --> 00:21:52,933
我也不确定岩石切割机能不能挖得动

874
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:55,866
所以我们徒手把它挖下来

875
00:21:56,733 --> 00:22:00,800
这就是我们需要的众多铱中的一份

876
00:22:01,166 --> 00:22:03,500
我们也可以使用 IC2 矿机

877
00:22:03,566 --> 00:22:06,466
但这些挖出来的垃圾比材料还多

878
00:22:07,266 --> 00:22:09,100
回到我们的小目标上

879
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:11,100
现在我们有了第二台计算机

880
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:15,133
我们要开始动手做 32 个线圈中的第一个了

881
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,000
这需要一些相当恶心的材料

882
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:21,300
但我觉得最恶心的是铱反射板

883
00:22:21,566 --> 00:22:27,366
这导致每个线圈都会消耗一个铱板和八个铍单元

884
00:22:27,766 --> 00:22:30,633
更不用提 32 个致密铜板了

885
00:22:30,633 --> 00:22:33,233
每个线圈总计要 4 组铜

886
00:22:33,766 --> 00:22:37,200
要得到额外的铜 我们可以离心岩浆

887
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:40,600
岩浆可以用岩浆制造机凭空做出来

888
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:47,066
目前 我们先重构并改造下界的抽岩浆系统并且开始离心岩浆

889
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:49,400
在我们积攒额外铜的同时

890
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:52,133
我们可以回去查查怎么做铍

891
00:22:52,533 --> 00:22:57,466
显然 只能通过电解末影珍珠或绿宝石来得到

892
00:22:58,066 --> 00:23:02,133
我觉得最可自动化的方式应该是用传送门机制

893
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:06,566
再一想 这自动化不了 也不好玩

894
00:23:07,066 --> 00:23:10,466
于是我们进入下一步 用研磨机

895
00:23:10,766 --> 00:23:12,100
设置好之后

896
00:23:12,133 --> 00:23:16,166
我们需要激怒一些末影人 勾引它们传送到机器的范围内

897
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:20,200
然后我们就从高空的视角看着它工作

898
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:23,933
这个装置还会产出一些怪物精华

899
00:23:24,166 --> 00:23:26,666
我们可以把它传送回基地

900
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:32,133
在那里我们可以用精华来驱动一个刷怪塔以产生更多的珍珠

901
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:34,466
看它们掉得有多快

902
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:37,200
有了一些可以开始加工的材料之后

903
00:23:37,266 --> 00:23:40,766
我们把它们打粉并电解

904
00:23:41,266 --> 00:23:43,400
于是我们终于有了铍

905
00:23:43,866 --> 00:23:47,500
我们还得到了一些氮和钾作为副产品

906
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:52,766
它们可以用来制造火药 做爆炸物来压缩铱板

907
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:56,533
最后 我们压缩了大量铜

908
00:23:56,666 --> 00:24:03,300
这样我们就能用中子反射板填满背包 再做成铱中子反射板

909
00:24:03,366 --> 00:24:06,366
唯一剩下的就是超导体了

910
00:24:06,466 --> 00:24:09,633
它还需要一个铱板

911
00:24:09,633 --> 00:24:13,566
所以 趁我们的组装机在工作能量流电路的时候

912
00:24:13,733 --> 00:24:16,533
我们回到末地去挖更多谢尔顿矿

913
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,933
在末地 我们还可以收集一些方钠石

914
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:23,200
可以通过电解获得钠

915
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,733
我们用它们来做钠钾冷却剂单元

916
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,700
现在我们材料都齐了

917
00:24:29,966 --> 00:24:31,800
我们可以做出超导体了

918
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:34,666
然后做出第一个聚变线圈

919
00:24:34,666 --> 00:24:41,533
终于 我们可以欣赏聚变控制计算机的合成过程 不用任何视频变速

920
00:24:41,766 --> 00:24:44,933
一开始我们先准备一个泥土甜甜圈

921
00:24:44,933 --> 00:24:50,100
然后把计算机作为第一个接触环内侧的最终方块放下去

922
00:24:50,566 --> 00:24:52,666
接下来我们要合成大量材料

923
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:54,800
我们从线圈开始

924
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:59,800
要做到这一点 第一步是踩在我们的充电板上

925
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:02,900
这样我们挂机的时候装甲可以保持充电

926
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,466
挂机了一段时间之后

927
00:25:05,666 --> 00:25:09,333
我们的离心机产出了一些铜和琥珀金

928
00:25:09,366 --> 00:25:11,366
这些都是线圈的基础材料

929
00:25:12,166 --> 00:25:16,100
铜是所有中子反射板都需要的

930
00:25:16,466 --> 00:25:19,666
而琥珀金将大大降低电路的成本

931
00:25:20,066 --> 00:25:24,100
但主要的问题将是超进阶机器方块

932
00:25:24,533 --> 00:25:27,866
我们需要两组的钛和两组的铬

933
00:25:28,266 --> 00:25:32,166
钛可以通过挂机囤积 UU 物质来做

934
00:25:32,366 --> 00:25:35,166
但铬只能用红宝石来做

935
00:25:35,566 --> 00:25:38,600
那我们就得挖 7 组红宝石

936
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,666
这不太现实

937
00:25:41,133 --> 00:25:44,166
那个 IC2 矿机似乎不能正常工作

938
00:25:44,366 --> 00:25:47,466
所以我们将把它的钻头升级为采石场

939
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:53,700
而且我们可以通过压缩我们农场污泥里产出的所有垃圾来获得额外的钻石

940
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,933
在钻石上面你种不了花

941
00:25:56,466 --> 00:26:03,300
但是你可以用污泥来制造钻石 再用钻石来合成采石场 它会挖到你所有需要的资源

942
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:07,866
我们放下它再加上一些超立方体来管理它的输入输出

943
00:26:08,166 --> 00:26:11,000
然后我们就能欣赏它的机器人搭建结构

944
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:13,166
框架完成之后

945
00:26:13,400 --> 00:26:17,466
切割头就会开始运行 耗电量大约相当于一台高炉

946
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,900
在超立方体的另一端

947
00:26:20,066 --> 00:26:23,266
我们在以最坏的方式管理输出

948
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:26,200
因为我找不到任何更好的 能和超立方体兼容的管道

949
00:26:26,666 --> 00:26:27,700
过了一段时间

950
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:31,500
我们已经填满了一个超级圆石箱子

951
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:35,200
我们可以看看从采石场中能获得什么

952
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:38,533
那么 我们可以把超立方体接上一个更好的分类装置

953
00:26:39,266 --> 00:26:45,600
我们会把装饰 mod 产生的所有垃圾存进桶里 那些东西会导致渲染问题和卡顿

954
00:26:45,733 --> 00:26:48,366
好东西留在这个箱子里

955
00:26:49,166 --> 00:26:52,800
然后 既然我们会有大量的多余石英

956
00:26:52,966 --> 00:26:58,300
我们可以用它来做输入总线和其他 AE1 的东西来自动化处理

957
00:26:58,766 --> 00:27:05,866
我们将投入相当于两个线圈份量的机器外壳去做一个量子箱 来看看我们到底挖了多少圆石

958
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:09,400
那么 是时候开始使用所有这些好东西了

959
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:13,266
我们还要改进我们的车间使其更自动化

960
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,100
不过 看起来在当年

961
00:27:16,366 --> 00:27:19,366
老资历们都是手工搓出好东西的

962
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:22,300
而不是用丑陋的自动化装置

963
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:28,200
从原版漏斗的缺失以及把东西从箱子和机器中取出来有多难就能看出来

964
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:31,100
试了很多次之后

965
00:27:31,266 --> 00:27:34,966
我放弃了从卷板机里取出板的尝试

966
00:27:35,366 --> 00:27:39,300
它上面有个东西看起来像新版自动输出的功能

967
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,933
但我手太笨了 死活搞不定

968
00:27:42,766 --> 00:27:45,066
不管怎样 我们做了第二台研磨机

969
00:27:45,066 --> 00:27:47,266
和旧的那台共用结构方块

970
00:27:47,466 --> 00:27:51,566
然后用我们能找到的最烂的管道给它加满水

971
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:54,333
接下来我们还做了一台电解机

972
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:59,333
现在我们让 AE1 合成一些输入总线和输出总线

973
00:27:59,966 --> 00:28:02,600
自动化热力膨胀的机器相当容易

974
00:28:02,766 --> 00:28:08,400
但这些老旧生锈的 GregTech 机器要求我们为每个输入找到正确的面

975
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:13,766
就这样我们几乎自动化了一切 像一个优秀的楚南工程师应该做的那样

976
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:17,266
唯一剩下的麻烦就是铱了

977
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:22,000
我知道的唯一能大量获取的方式就是 UU 物质

978
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:27,766
然而 自从我们建成物质制造机以来只做出了 3 个

979
00:28:27,766 --> 00:28:30,666
所以 或许我们可以先做一个聚变反应堆

980
00:28:31,266 --> 00:28:33,700
或者我们可以做一个终极太阳能板

981
00:28:33,700 --> 00:28:37,133
这样就能让用不上的铀有更长期的用途

982
00:28:37,533 --> 00:28:38,600
可能不做也好

983
00:28:38,866 --> 00:28:42,466
因为那需要半个聚变反应堆份量的铱

984
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:46,100
真空反应堆倒是能发不少电

985
00:28:46,766 --> 00:28:51,800
然而 真空冷冻机会用掉所有那些电力去冷却冷却剂单元

986
00:28:52,333 --> 00:28:54,900
所以我们必须选择更高效的方案

987
00:28:55,266 --> 00:28:58,166
于是我们就有了一个简易粗糙的钚反应堆

988
00:28:58,166 --> 00:29:01,566
发电大约相当于两台 RC 锅炉

989
00:29:02,100 --> 00:29:05,966
我们不会用四联燃料棒 因为那太耗铜了

990
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:08,566
等我们的采石场挖完之后

991
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:12,500
我们再做一个 这样它在下一个工地就不会孤单了

992
00:29:13,066 --> 00:29:14,000
双倍的采石场

993
00:29:14,266 --> 00:29:15,066
双倍的快乐

994
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:18,966
现在是时候挂机囤积资源了

995
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:20,600
等我们有了足够的量

996
00:29:20,700 --> 00:29:24,500
我们就可以通过以下自动化序列开始改进我们的基地了

997
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:52,900
甜甜圈刚完成

998
00:33:52,900 --> 00:33:55,333
我们就加上两个输入材料注射器

999
00:33:55,666 --> 00:33:58,533
一个材料输出器和四个能量注射器

1000
00:33:59,466 --> 00:34:04,533
位置和 GTNH 聚变反应堆的一样

1001
00:34:04,533 --> 00:34:09,433
接下来 接上电源等待反应堆内部缓冲充能

1002
00:34:09,433 --> 00:34:13,333
以我们目前的发电量 大概需要一刻钟

1003
00:34:14,166 --> 00:34:15,000
等待期间

1004
00:34:15,266 --> 00:34:16,733
我们准备一下燃料

1005
00:34:16,766 --> 00:34:20,266
我们从电解水获得氢开始

1006
00:34:21,066 --> 00:34:24,100
接下来离心分离出一些氘

1007
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:27,733
最后 用氘做出一些氚

1008
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:31,700
当我们聚变氘和氚的时候

1009
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:34,866
我们会得到一些氦等离子体

1010
00:34:34,866 --> 00:34:38,300
要使用它 需要一台等离子发电机

1011
00:34:38,966 --> 00:34:42,266
那台机器包括一些钨钢材料

1012
00:34:42,266 --> 00:34:47,066
正如 Tooltip 所说的 钨钢必须进行真空硬化

1013
00:34:47,066 --> 00:34:49,533
所以在钨钢烧制的期间

1014
00:34:49,666 --> 00:34:52,166
我们要做一台真空冷冻机

1015
00:34:52,966 --> 00:34:56,133
如预期的那样 这是一台多方块机器

1016
00:34:57,133 --> 00:34:59,566
但用的还是同样的机器外壳

1017
00:34:59,566 --> 00:35:01,800
我们很快就建好了

1018
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:05,966
与此同时 我们的聚变反应堆充到了四分之一的电量

1019
00:35:06,666 --> 00:35:09,166
但这可能就是反应堆的上限了

1020
00:35:09,333 --> 00:35:13,400
因为能量注射器上限是 16 个 我们只有 4 个

1021
00:35:14,533 --> 00:35:18,600
那么试试给它喂点燃料看看它能不能工作

1022
00:35:19,266 --> 00:35:21,000
灯没有亮

1023
00:35:21,100 --> 00:35:23,366
但我们损失了所有储存的能量

1024
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:27,400
不过看起来我们设法得到了一单元等离子体

1025
00:35:27,666 --> 00:35:29,466
为了保持持续聚变

1026
00:35:29,500 --> 00:35:31,866
我们再多做一个能量注射器

1027
00:35:32,166 --> 00:35:33,900
并把它装到线圈上

1028
00:35:34,333 --> 00:35:36,533
在再次缓冲足够能量之后

1029
00:35:36,666 --> 00:35:38,000
我们丢进燃料

1030
00:35:38,533 --> 00:35:40,866
这次灯亮了

1031
00:35:40,866 --> 00:35:44,600
我们正在持续产生氦等离子体流

1032
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:46,366
除了热等离子体

1033
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,566
我们也有热钨钢

1034
00:35:48,733 --> 00:35:52,366
一半热钨钢应该放进真空冷冻机

1035
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,800
这样我们就有了等离子发电机

1036
00:35:54,800 --> 00:35:57,933
我们把它放在物质制造机旁边

1037
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,766
最后 喂它一些等离子体

1038
00:36:00,766 --> 00:36:03,800
这样我们终于能有一个像样的 UU 物质生产了

1039
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:09,600
我们的物质制造机确实接收了太多能量 以至于它都来不及工作那么快

1040
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,966
它的能量缓冲正在被充满

1041
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,966
而且 你大概也注意到了

1042
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:17,733
这不仅仅是一台等离子发电机的功率

1043
00:36:18,100 --> 00:36:21,133
其实 还包括墙上那些新发电机的功率

1044
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:27,566
唯一剩下要做的事就是 在我们的 AE1 系统中展示一下我们的圆石收藏

1045
00:36:27,966 --> 00:36:29,566
所以我们做了一个存储总线

1046
00:36:29,566 --> 00:36:31,400
然后把它连接到量子箱子
